// ── Your personal build settings ───────────────────────────────────────────
// Copy this file to  LocalConfig.xcconfig  (same folder, drop the ".example")
// and fill in your own values. LocalConfig.xcconfig is gitignored, so nothing
// personal is ever committed.
//
// After editing, regenerate the Xcode project:   ./scripts/generate-project.sh
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// 1) A bundle ID that is UNIQUE TO YOU.
//    Apple requires every App ID / App Group to be globally unique, so use a
//    reverse-DNS string based on a domain or name YOU control: letters,
//    numbers, hyphens and dots only. The widgets' ID and the App Group are
//    derived from this automatically.
//    Examples:  com.janesmith.fabolus   org.yourdomain.fabolus
APP_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.fabolus

// 2) Your Apple Developer Team ID (10 characters), or nothing after the "="
//    to pick your Team in Xcode's Signing & Capabilities tab instead (you then
//    pick it again each time you regenerate the project).
//    Paid account: developer.apple.com/account → Membership details.
//    Free account: make an Apple Development certificate (Xcode → Settings →
//    Accounts → your team → Manage Certificates… → + → Apple Development), then
//    run in Terminal:
//      security find-certificate -c "Apple Development" -p | openssl x509 -noout -subject
//    The Team ID is the 10 characters after "OU=".
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
